Conservatory is DONE (THE FINAL BLITZ).

Date: 2026-09-15 (v0.8.0 tagged and released the same day).

What shipped in the blitz (commit range 1e66159..2eec79f on main, this
commit closing it; tag v0.8.0 on the release commit 9d4fc2f):

- The backup/restore crash-window repair: restore now checkpoints the live
  WAL before the rename commit point and sweeps the emptied sidecars after
  it, refusing a busy database; three regression tests pin the windows.
- The move preview's skipped-conflict promise is the behavior, the
  importers' pre-commit integrity pair (music MissingSource pre-check via
  the mover's own plan; audiobook recovery before any DB write), the
  threading lane (the scoped-move and re-shelve flows off the GTK thread,
  mover file ops on the blocking pool, 46 silent block_on sites surfaced
  through ui::log_worker_err), and the podcast feed body cap (32 MiB).
- The docs-truth cluster, the version carriers, the crate recount, the
  milestone table, the comment truth pass (MED + LOW), the docs-staleness
  tail, and the mechanical em-dash recast (172 separators).
- GitHub: Releases for v0.7.0 plus the v0.5.0/v0.4.5/v0.4.4 backfill
  (Latest = v0.8.0), release.yml minting future Releases from tag
  messages, the meson packaging validators in CI, the Atrium-shape ci.yml
  sync (SHA pins, permissions, concurrency, setup-uv v10, VERSION guard),
  actions-only dependabot, SECURITY.md + private vulnerability reporting
  + minimal issue templates.
- Housekeeping per Brandon's gate answers (the .gitkeep trio, the
  GSettings gitignore block, /.flatpak-builder/, URL casing, local
  .claude residue).
- The final-audit roadmap block fully ticked, and the L4 features slotted
  in the roadmap's "Slotted features (the final audit's L4)" section.

Reopen conditions (the recorded future work; none of it is open agent
work):

- The 50k-library real-data gate sessions (memory gate + move-safety
